  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to grow thick, to be overgrown",
      "explanation": "For plants, grass, or trees to grow densely."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "03924_shigeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{夏|なつ}になると{草|くさ}が{茂|しげ}る。",
      "english": "The grass grows thick when summer comes.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03924_shigeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{木|き}が{茂|しげ}って{日陰|ひかげ}ができた。",
      "english": "The trees grew thick and created shade.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03924_shigeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{庭|にわ}に{雑草|ざっそう}が{茂|しげ}っている。",
      "english": "Weeds are growing thick in the garden.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03924_shigeru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{山道|やまみち}の{両側|りょうがわ}に{木|き}が{茂|しげ}っていて{暗|くら}かった。",
      "english": "Trees grew thick on both sides of the mountain path and it was dark.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03924_shigeru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{手入|てい}れをしないと、{庭|にわ}はすぐに{草|くさ}が{茂|しげ}ってしまう。",
      "english": "If you don't maintain it, the garden quickly becomes overgrown with grass.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{茂|しげ}る means for vegetation to grow thickly or luxuriantly.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし})\n- No common transitive pair\n- Pattern: Xが{茂|しげ}る\n\nASPECT:\n- {茂|しげ}っている: Is overgrown (resulting state)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {草|くさ}が{茂|しげ}る (grass grows thick)\n- {木|き}が{茂|しげ}る (trees grow thick)\n- うっそうと{茂|しげ}る (to grow luxuriantly)\n- {生|お}い{茂|しげ}る (to grow thickly, to be overgrown)\n\nRELATED VOCABULARY:\n- {生|は}える (to grow, sprout)\n- {伸|の}びる (to grow, extend)",
